 "headline": "Both calendar rules pass the fixed test (Fosback seasonality on SPY, PF 1.56 after publication; Kaeppel's Monthly 10 on DIA, PF 1.57), but after publication they beat random entry days only weakly (z 0.5 and 1.0): most of their profit is simply being invested in a rising market, and they return less than buy and hold (4.9% and 8.2% a year vs 14% and 13%). Grossmann's VXX-short rules (claimed 96% a year) fell from 53\u201371% a year before publication to 9\u201316% after, with 45\u201365% drawdowns. The lunar effect vanished after 2001. Best winner stays round 3's IBS rule on QQQ."
